course: dictionary
lesson: 441
title: The archerfish and its water jet
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: An archerfish is a small fish that lives in warm rivers and mangroves in Asia and northern Australia. It hunts insects that sit on leaves above the water. It cannot climb up to them, so it uses a clever trick: it shoots a jet of water from its mouth to knock the insect down.
explain: «Archerfish shoot jets of water to knock insects into the water.» Once the insect falls in, the fish swims over and eats it. The name fits well, because like an archer with a bow, the fish takes careful aim before it shoots.
explain: Aiming is harder than it looks. Water bends light where it meets air, so the insect seems to be in a different place from where it really is. Yet the archerfish still hits its target. This makes it a great example of an animal adaptation, a body part or skill that helps an animal survive.
fact: An archerfish is a small fish from warm rivers and mangroves.
fact: Archerfish live in Asia and northern Australia.
fact: An archerfish shoots a jet of water from its mouth to knock insects off leaves above the water.
fact: After the insect falls into the water, the archerfish swims over and eats it.
fact: Water bends light, so things look as if they are in a different place, but archerfish still aim correctly.
exercise: What is an archerfish? | A fish that lives deep in the sea | A tiny insect that lives on leaves | *A small fish that lives in warm rivers and mangroves | A large bird that hunts in cold forests
exercise: «Archerfish shoot jets of water to knock insects into the water.» What does the jet of water do? | It puts out a fire | It washes the leaf clean | It cools the insect down | *It knocks an insect off a leaf so it falls into the water
exercise: Why is it tricky for an archerfish to aim? | Insects always hide under water | Fish cannot move their heads | *Water bends light, so the insect looks like it is in a different place | Archerfish cannot see at all
test: What does the archerfish do after the insect falls into the water? | *Swims over and eats it | Flies up to the leaf | Sleeps under a rock | Builds a nest
test: Why is the archerfish an example of an animal adaptation? | It is the same as every other fish | *It has a body and skill that help it catch food | It lives on land like a bird | It has no body parts at all
exam: Which best describes where archerfish live? | *Warm rivers and mangroves in Asia and northern Australia | High mountains in Europe | Dry deserts in Africa | Cold seas near the North Pole
